    "contract": [
      "Serialize cooperating processes mutations for each credential with a user-scoped authority independent of settings profile/TMP overrides. Bound lock admission without blocking the GUI.",
      "Associate each adoption with an across-process version, including identical-value writes; compare it while holding authority through backend completion.",
      "Preserve authority across closed windows and late backend completions; never treat timeout/cancellation as proof a write cannot still commit.",
      "Exercise writer crash, pending/failed writes, metadata/backend disagreement, stale/foreign lock ownership, read/delete races and caller deletion. Keep secrets only in the OS keychain.",
      "Qualify the actual OS backends on Windows/macOS/Linux, including crash/late-completion behavior. Do not promote component tests to a whole-store atomicity claim."
    ]
